1. Searching
Searching means finding whether a particular element exists in a collection and, if it exists, finding its position.
Example:
Array = [10, 25, 30, 45, 50]
Search for 30.
30 is present at index 2

There are two important searching techniques:
Linear Search
Binary Search
A. Linear Search
Linear search checks elements one by one from the beginning.
Example:
[10, 25, 30, 45, 50]
 ↑
Check 10 → No

[10, 25, 30, 45, 50]
     ↑
Check 25 → No

[10, 25, 30, 45, 50]
         ↑
Check 30 → Yes

JAVA CODE:
int[] arr = {10, 25, 30, 45, 50};
int target = 30;

for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] == target) {
        System.out.println("Found at index " + i);
        break;
    }
}

Complexity
Best case: O(1) → element is first
Worst case: O(n) → element is last/not present
Space: O(1)
